  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Merge DataFrames** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_merge_dataframes(left: list, right: list, on: str, how: str = 'inner') -> list:\n    df = pd.merge(pd.DataFrame(left), pd.DataFrame(right), on=on, how=how)\n    return df.where(pd.notnull(df), None).to_dict(orient='records')\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
